    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d478-a1">

                <pb facs="0572" n="484" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg484"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Mariscal to Mr.
                            Clayton.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-02-12"><hi rendition="#italic">February 12,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Ambassador</hi>: I had the honor to receive the
                    note of January 27 last in which your excellency was pleased to ask the
                    intervention of this department to procure the prompt termination of the suits
                    brought against the engineers of the Sonora Railway Company, F. Gordon and C. O.
                    Bean, for damages caused by trains under their charge, respectively.</p>
                <p>With regard to the case of Bean I have the honor to transmit to your excellency
                    herewith a copy of a report upon the same made by the district judge of Nogales
                    on December 21 last, by which it appears that the said authority dismissed the
                    said case, the decision in the same having been referred to the third circuit
                    court for review. I have requested the prompt dispatch of this matter by the
                    proper authority.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I beg, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Igno, Mariscal.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
